# The stone60 route (#210): the pause route's boot, title and New Game (pause-ws.pad, play from
# 6,349), a walk from Artisans' start across the lawn and a jump into Stone Hill's portal (6,422 on:
# the portal's sky up close, then gamestate 1, the fly-in, 6,805 to 7,225, and the entrance
# animation), Stone Hill play from 7,293: up the hill into the ram, which butts Spyro (about 7,780:
# the stars round him are particle case-3 quads, ParticlesDraw's screen-facing quads), on round the
# stone block, then run, flame, charge, jump and glide twice (8,509 to 9,349; #209's route S's
# actions). Absolute vblanks, no pokes: steered on the linux32 host at 60 Hz logic (--tick60,
# tools/steer.py step sessions), so with virtual vblanks (no REALTIME=1) every run plays the same.
# The same file runs on the host:
#   spyro --disc disc/files --pad tools/vita/hw-routes/stone60.pad --tick60 --widescreen \
#     --draw-distance 2 --vcache --frames 9500 --shot-every 100 --shot-dir DIR
# and in Vita3K with stone60.cfg's settings (autopilot/config.json's stone60 route).
